WEBVTT

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.350
<i>I already knew what we would find, but...</i>

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.600
Hey! Is anybody out there?

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:24.020
Is anyone alive out there? Hey!

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.110
-I'm going to swim out there.
-What?

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:31.650
Dude, that water can't be very clean.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.330
<i>The ruins of the city
and the remains of the dead...</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.040
<i>There must be a ton of them down here.</i>

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.000
<i>Hana as well?</i>

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.000
<i>I could... join her.</i>

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:50.590
It's hard to think of what to do
when the optimistic guy is

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.460
the one getting depressed.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.470
Arashi...

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:57.090
Oh, your house wasn't far from here,
right? In Saitama--

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:02.220
No way! We never saw
a single fish this whole time.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:04.770
Arashi!

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.370
HEAVY SNOW

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.120
Team Winter?

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.000
Yes.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.710
What happened to the others?

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:57.300
I'm the only one left.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:00.970
How did you end up alone?

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.720
You...

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:09.520
I've been surviving on my own
for over 15 years now.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:11.940
Fifteen years?

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.860
Well, we're really happy
we found you out here. Right?

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:17.110
But just keep those dogs
away from me, okay?

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.400
You're afraid of dogs?

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.780
Don't you know how fearsome dogs are?

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:24.410
Those things will bite you!

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.330
It's almost the rainy season.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.870
<i>Dangerous creatures will start appearing.</i>

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.500
-Ready. Go.
-Ready. Go.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.090
It's been flooded with water.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.470
And we worked so hard to find it.

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:47.140
Hold on.
These flashlights are waterproof, right?

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.220
I'll go check it out.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:49.890
Be careful, Hana.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.480
<i>It splits? Which way do I go?</i>

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.200
<i>This rope isn't very old.</i>

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.160
<i>Someone must have been here recently.</i>

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:15.040
What is this place?

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.040
A storage room?

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:19.500
There's food.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:21.970
There are tools over here.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.800
Look.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:24.760
What?

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.390
"Greetings, we are from Team Summer B.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:34.230
The other members of our group are
in Kyushu at the shelter on Mt. Yufu.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:38.320
If anyone else comes and finds this note,
please leave us a sign.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.860
We hope to meet you one day.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.400
Natsu Iwashimizu."

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.110
Team Summer B?

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:45.780
So other teams do exist.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:49.790
Mt. Yufu in Kyushu is another one of
the seven regional Fuji mountains.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:53.000
Then everything
that Old Man Yanagi told us was true.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:59.750
Hana, this is a huge find for us.
Let's keep pushing on.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.170
Okay.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:02.880
Check this out.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:05.840
Books.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:07.680
Oh, wow!

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:09.010
A bunch of how-to books.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.350
Astronomy guides, meteorology guides,
even encyclopedias.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:15.230
All I see are a bunch of old books.

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.690
-Didn't they leave any comics?
-Books... I almost forgot.

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:20.360
For some reason,
there was one in my bag too.

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:22.320
It's the second half of <i>Robinson Crusoe</i>.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:23.610
Just the second half?

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.150
I was borrowing it.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.530
I already read the first half
and gave it back.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.530
Gather round!

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:34.700
I want you all to hear me out. I believe
we need to change our way of thinking.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:40.040
Up until now, we've all thought about
returning to our everyday lives.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:44.170
But those lives don't exist anymore.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:49.010
We really did end up surviving
the apocalypse.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:53.560
In other words, you're saying we have to
think about how to live here.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:56.270
<i>Live here?</i>

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:02.480
Arashi...

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:04.860
<i>Hana.</i>

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:07.360
Mom... Dad...

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.530
Everyone is gone.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.250
<i>What meaning is there in continuing on?</i>

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.040
<i>What's the point?</i>

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.800
I found rice in the storage shelter,
so I cooked some.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:29.510
Everyone is here, so let's eat.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.430
-Thanks for the meal.
-Thanks for the meal.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.560
It feels like forever since I had rice.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:35.930
It's delicious.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:37.480
Oh, that's right.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:41.100
Earlier, I found a place
with hot water coming out of the ground.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:43.190
A hot spring? Awesome.

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:46.190
I hate taking baths,
so I don't really care.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:47.570
What a slob.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:51.870
-Haru, show me where it is after dinner.
-<i>A bath and dinner.</i>

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:54.160
-<i>I guess that's all I really needed.</i>
-It's already dark.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.370
Wouldn't tomorrow be better?

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:56.830
Let's all go tomorrow.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:57.910
<i>I feel alive.</i>

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.080
<i>I'm still alive.</i>

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:04.630
<i>Please let Arashi be alive, too.</i>

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:07.050
<i>Please.</i>

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:15.060
Hey, everybody.

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.810
What do you think about making this
our base?

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:21.310
From here, we can gradually
explore outward.

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:24.520
We'll use Robinson Crusoe as our guide.

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:34.700
We're better off dead.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.330
-Arashi.
-What?

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.710
Let's run while we've got the chance.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:43.290
Hey, Natsu. Wake up.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:46.500
What? We're going to leave
without saying anything?

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.050
He seemed like a nice person.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:51.300
Jeez, can't you tell the good
from the bad?

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:54.050
Are you sure you're not just afraid
of his dogs, Semimaru?

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.100
What?

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:58.260
The fact that he's the only survivor is
a huge red flag.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:02.100
They might have killed each other,
or worse, eaten each other.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:07.770
Anyway, there's no way someone can
stay sane after 15 years in this place.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:10.320
Did you forget about Team Autumn?

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.360
I agree with Semimaru. Let's go.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:14.700
Arashi...

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:18.490
Quietly. Very quietly.

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.080
Hey, hurry up.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.000
Right.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.510
<i>So I'm alone again?</i>

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:44.310
<i>Fifteen years ago, we awoke to...</i>

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:46.270
Hey, look.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:48.610
Someone dug up the bodies we buried.

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:50.280
Who would do this?

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.320
Is that a wolf? A dog?

00:08:57.410 --> 00:09:00.910
You don't think this is what
killed Mutsuki and dug up the graves?

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.500
Back away. Slowly.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:09.500
Mr. Kumakawa.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.010
This is the thing that ate the others.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:16.260
It eats people.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:23.480
Throw it, Taka.

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:24.850
What? At the tiger?

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:25.850
No, at me.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.440
A fastball, right down the middle. Now!

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.580
Did that do it?

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:42.490
But...

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:45.120
<i>Shortly after we awoke in Hokkaido,</i>

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:49.000
<i>only three of us were left in Team Winter.</i>

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:56.010
Looks like you got into a fight
with that tiger thing, too.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:58.680
Leave it be. It's dangerous.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:00.800
<i>We set out northeast.</i>

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:05.850
<i>Supplies were waiting for us at one
of the seven Fuji mountains, Mt. Meakan.</i>

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:07.940
<i>That's what our guide,
Mr. Kumakawa, had said.</i>

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.980
Man, I want to play some baseball.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:13.230
Both of you were on the baseball team
in high school, right?

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:14.530
That's right.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:18.780
I was the best shortstop of the century,
and a real slugger too.

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:22.330
They say a pitcher as good as this guy
only comes around once every 50 years.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.410
He was the star of the Koshien Tournament.

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:26.250
I'm not that remarkable.

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:32.750
Damn, I wish they had put
some equipment in our bags.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:34.630
You can't do much
with just a ball and a cap.

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:38.380
There was nothing related to baseball
in my bag.

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:41.470
I wish they hadn't bothered putting
any mementos in our bags.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.930
Mine had a stage dress inside.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:47.100
I wish they used the space
for a chocolate bar.

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:48.270
A stage dress?

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:50.730
I performed traditional Japanese dancing.

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:53.440
But I certainly can't do that here.

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:58.030
Throw a rock. Hit them with it, Taka.

00:10:58.440 --> 00:10:59.400
Right.

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:06.790
That was close.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.710
What's wrong, Mr. Koshien Tournament Star?

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:10.500
That Koshien Tournament...

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:14.250
We ended up losing the big game
because I threw a wild pitch.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:15.750
What?

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:18.050
When I'm under pressure,
I just can't pitch very well.

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:19.510
You're wrong.

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:21.380
Your team's batting was the real problem.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:24.850
If I had been on your team,
there's no doubt we would be the champs.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.930
Pitch to me.
Just like how you did with the tiger.

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:35.770
You hit it!

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:40.400
Looks like your bat control is
even better than they say, Fubuki.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:41.320
What?

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.450
What? Have you heard of us before?

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:48.040
Actually, I'm a huge fan
of high school baseball.

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:50.830
Naturally, I know all about you two.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.120
From your favorite foods,
right down to your shoe sizes.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.920
Seriously? You should have said something.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.630
That's why, to be honest,

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:00.720
I'm really happy I ended up with you two.

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:04.220
At the very least, I already know

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:07.470
you both put your heart
and soul into baseball.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:12.640
I believe people who dedicate themselves
to one thing are trustworthy.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:18.520
Maybe it's that wolf-dog.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:22.150
You treated its wound earlier,
so now it's probably following us.

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:29.330
Pitch it here.

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.080
It won't get past me.

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:32.160
Sorry,

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:34.580
I just don't have enough confidence.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:35.880
Don't have confidence?

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:37.170
Are you serious?

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:39.670
-Don't give me that crap!
-Sorry!

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:40.880
Listen here!

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:44.840
I played baseball in little league,
middle school, and high school,

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:48.350
but I've never met a single pitcher
who wasn't full of grit!

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:52.890
Man, how can a guy who won ten games
at Koshien spout crap like that?

00:12:57.650 --> 00:13:01.860
I read that second basemen and shortstops
usually struggle to have compassion.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:02.860
Ms. Mitsuru?

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:07.280
Despite what you may think,
Fubuki is really looking out for you.

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:14.120
I see.

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:21.380
That dog's barking, it sounds different.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:22.300
What's up?

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:26.930
This field has turned into a river.

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:28.720
How is this possible?

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:31.470
We won't last long here.
Get your stuff together.

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:33.600
Do you have the rope tied tightly?

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:35.520
Yes.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:36.980
Let's move.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:40.940
What is it?

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:42.610
I can't swim.

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:45.030
We're not swimming.
We're just going to walk across.

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:47.660
-Go on without me.
-No way.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:50.320
Get a hold of yourself.
If you stay here, you'll die.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:52.410
But I'm too weak.

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:54.000
Listen to me, Taka.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:57.790
I stood on the mound
only once during an official game.

00:13:58.420 --> 00:13:59.290
What?

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:00.670
My legs were trembling.

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:04.670
I realized that pitchers stood in
the scariest place on the field.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:08.630
They fight alone,
facing immense pressure and fear.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:10.800
I couldn't do it. I was afraid.

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:12.680
I gained a newfound respect for them.

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:13.890
That's when I made up my mind

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:16.140
to stand firm behind them.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:18.310
I would support them
with everything I've got.

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:19.770
You'll be fine!

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:22.190
As long as I'm here,
you can make it, Taka!

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.490
I'm also with you. Don't worry.

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:27.240
Okay.

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:32.620
Taka, why do you think I've been able
to hit all of your pitches so far?

00:14:33.410 --> 00:14:36.500
Because you've always been the pitcher
I would use to do mental imagery training.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.660
Hitting your pitches has
always been my dream.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:42.090
Mitsuru! Taka!

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:46.710
Let's go. We're going to make it.

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:48.880
The three of us, together!

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:52.390
<i>We'll find a way to survive,</i>

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:54.060
<i>all three of us.</i>

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:56.560
It's so cold. I'm freezing.

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:59.350
At this rate, we'll die from exposure.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:05.610
We should tear up my stage dress
and use it to bundle up.

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:11.570
-Keep moving.
-Right.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:15.160
Those aren't a dog's footprints.

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:19.710
How did it go, Taka?

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:22.540
Good. I found potatoes.

00:15:31.510 --> 00:15:32.430
That's the tiger.

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:34.390
It's been tracking us this whole time.

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:37.770
Mitsuru! Taka! Run for it!

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:38.680
Fubuki?

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:40.890
I'll handle this.

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.600
I won't let it get past me.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:47.860
-I'll keep you both safe, no matter what.
-Fubuki!

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:51.400
-Fubuki!
-Taka!

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:53.280
Mitsuru! Get out of here!

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:54.780
I'll join up with you later.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:58.330
We're going to survive this! Together!

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:00.790
Go!

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:02.290
Fubuki!

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:06.170
Come on!
This our chance to get out of here.

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:07.300
But...

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:08.460
Just come on!

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:20.430
It's okay. The wound isn't deep.

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:22.560
Taka, you'll be fine.

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:41.410
Before all this, I was supposed to
perform the crane dance.

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:43.250
"Crane"?

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:45.330
It's based on <i>The Grateful Crane</i>.

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.710
A crane named Tsu fell in love with
a man named Yohyo,

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:50.960
and thought they could be together...

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:53.090
forever.

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:57.600
<i>However, the end came.</i>

00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:02.180
<i>Tsu had to leave him.</i>

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:05.190
<i>They could no longer stay together.</i>

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:07.860
Ms. Mitsuru...

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:25.750
<i>Oh, how beautiful...</i>

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:46.890
Don't leave me all alone!

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:58.360
Why? Why am I still alive?

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:01.080
Do I have to keep on living?

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:03.870
Can't I...

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:06.500
just die already?

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.830
Please let me die.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:21.050
Fubuki...

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:25.850
Don't leave me behind.

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:28.440
But you were dead.

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:30.190
There was so much blood.

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:32.610
Most of that was the tiger's blood.

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:35.400
Fubuki. Ms. Mitsuru, she...

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:38.400
Ms. Mitsuru is...

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:41.700
<i>Only the two of us were left.</i>

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:47.540
Are you okay?

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:49.670
I'm fine. Don't worry.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:54.710
<i>Fubuki sometimes looked like
he was in pain from his wounds.</i>

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:57.840
Maybe it's because I almost died,
but my sense of smell has improved.

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:00.890
I have a feeling it can
help us find our way.

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:02.640
<i>This time, it's my turn.</i>

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:05.470
<i>I'll protect Fubuki no matter what.</i>

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:18.360
Man, you look nothing like you did on TV
at the Koshien Tournament.

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:21.200
Yes, because I'm really just
a big and clumsy scaredy-cat.

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:22.570
That's not true at all.

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:26.080
Living life is
no different from playing baseball.

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:26.990
What?

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:30.960
You used all your strength,
all your senses, and your intuition

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:33.250
to play and win all those games.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:38.380
It was a fierce tournament,
and right now is no different.

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:42.930
Wherever you have to fight,
that's the same as being on the mound.

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:44.890
<i>We'll survive</i>

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:46.930
<i>using all of our strength,</i>

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:48.680
<i>all our senses,</i>

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:50.480
<i>and our intuition.</i>

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:52.940
<i>We'll prepare and we'll practice.</i>

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:55.900
<i>We'll set goals and plan ahead,</i>

00:19:55.980 --> 00:19:57.820
<i>analyze and decide,</i>

00:19:57.900 --> 00:19:59.190
<i>fight and win!</i>

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:03.530
<i>Living life really is
the same as playing baseball.</i>

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.080
It's that tiger again.

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:09.370
Fubuki! Get back!

00:20:16.920 --> 00:20:18.000
<i>This tiger is...</i>

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:20.590
<i>just trying to stay alive.</i>

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:24.510
Fubuki, look at that.

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:25.890
We made it!

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:27.930
We're still alive.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:29.890
We haven't lost yet.

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:31.430
Right, Fubuki?

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:33.690
Right. Do your best, Taka.

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:36.400
Keep fighting out there on the mound.

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:38.650
Fubuki?

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:46.410
<i>Back when that tiger attacked Fubuki,
he was killed.</i>

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:49.990
<i>The one who came with me all this way
was actually you.</i>

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:53.080
<i>I didn't want to believe
that Fubuki was dead.</i>

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:55.330
<i>I didn't think I could go on without him.</i>

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:59.210
<i>Thank you for staying with me
this whole time.</i>

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:02.550
<i>Thank you for making sure
I made it this far.</i>

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:03.550
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:07.140
<i>Despite all these wounds,
you kept holding on.</i>

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:12.140
You were their mother?

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:16.560
Will you come with me?

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:28.620
Those three said
they were from Team Summer.

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:31.330
There might still be others out there.

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:34.790
I want to be of help,

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:39.670
but finding someone in this world
who's still willing to trust

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:42.380
is going to be very difficult.

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:46.510
Okay, let's do a roll-call.

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:47.510
Glove.

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:48.550
Bat.

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:50.220
Diamond.

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:51.760
Battery.

00:21:53.140 --> 00:21:54.980
Diamond? Battery?

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:57.900
Diamond. Battery.

00:21:57.980 --> 00:21:59.310
<i>When did we get separated?</i>

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:01.440
-<i>The weak always fall prey.</i>
-Diamond!

00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:04.440
<i>I've seen it happen firsthand
so many times.</i>

00:22:04.530 --> 00:22:05.570
Battery!

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:13.450
Get away from that monster!

00:22:22.090 --> 00:22:24.130
Don't chase it! Its pack will be nearby.

00:22:25.880 --> 00:22:27.550
Another person.

00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:30.840
Hello.

00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:33.680
Hello.

00:22:33.850 --> 00:22:35.100
<i>She smiled.</i>

00:22:35.850 --> 00:22:39.900
<i>I believed I had survived all this time
to meet her.</i>
